# Question 1
- Create a `PairwiseAligner` object and configure it with custom scoring parameters to align two DNA sequences `"ACCGT"` and `"ACGT"`. Print out the alignment details and score. 

    <span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Use `Align.PairwiseAligner()`, set `match_score`, `mismatch_score`, `open_gap_score`, and `extend_gap_score` - play around with different scoring parameters
<br></br>

# Question 2
- Read a multiple sequence alignment from a Clustal format file `"data/protein_alignment.clustal"` and print out the length of the alignment and the sequence for each record. 

    <span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Use `AlignIO.read()` with `"clustal"` format, iterate through records to display details
<br></br>

# Question 3
- Identify and extract all conserved columns from a multiple sequence alignment loaded from `"data/gene_family.clustal"`.

